From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: cix: keep the Sky1 VPU APB clock enabled

The VPU register aperture at 0x14240000 is inaccessible when its APB
clock is gated.  Firmware describes SCMI clock 67 (vpu_apbclk) to the
VPU consumer as "vpu_clk", but keeping only the clkdev lookup does not
keep the gate enabled before the consumer's first register access.

Take an enable reference after all CLKT entries have been installed and
hold it for the lifetime of the CIXHA010 provider.  This is intentionally
limited to the VPU connection and is safe with the consumer's own
reference-counted enable/disable calls.

This is a conservative platform-layer workaround while the 7.2 clock
shutdown/SCMI ordering difference from the working 7.0.12 image is being
isolated on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
index 4c5ca954da00..46c6768b8c8f 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@ static void sky1_clkdev_drop(void *data)
 	clkdev_drop(data);
 }
 
+static void sky1_clk_disable_unprepare_put(void *data)
+{
+	struct clk *clk = data;
+
+	clk_disable_unprepare(clk);
+	clk_put(clk);
+}
+
 static int sky1_parse_clkt_entry(struct sky1_acpi_clk *priv,
 				 const char *consumer_name,
 				 union acpi_object *entry)
@@ -153,6 +160,8 @@ static int sky1_acpi_clk_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct sky1_acpi_clk *priv;
 	acpi_status status;
+	struct clk *vpu_apbclk;
+	int ret;
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!priv)
@@ -172,6 +181,28 @@ static int sky1_acpi_clk_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
 				     "No SCMI clocks mapped yet\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * The VPU's sole CLKT entry maps SCMI clock 67 (vpu_apbclk) as
+	 * CIXH3010:00 / vpu_clk.  Keep its register-bus gate open so the
+	 * first access to the VPU aperture cannot race clock shutdown.
+	 */
+	vpu_apbclk = clk_get_sys("CIXH3010:00", "vpu_clk");
+	if (IS_ERR(vpu_apbclk))
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(vpu_apbclk),
+				     "VPU APB clock is not mapped\n");
+
+	ret = clk_prepare_enable(vpu_apbclk);
+	if (ret) {
+		clk_put(vpu_apbclk);
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
+				     "Failed to enable VPU APB clock\n");
+	}
+
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(&pdev->dev,
+				       sky1_clk_disable_unprepare_put, vpu_apbclk);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "Mapped %d ACPI clock lookup entries\n",
 		 priv->mapped);
 	return 0;
-- 
2.51.0
